{
  "headline": "December lean hogs fell $1.87 Wednesday to $49.93",
  "lead": "December lean hogs settled at $49.925 on Wednesday, down 3.6% from Tuesday's $51.80 settle. Cash pork cutout was $66.98 per hundredweight, up $0.74, so packers are still paying less for hogs while pork itself is holding. Markets are closed today for Thanksgiving.",
  "one_number": {
    "value": "492,000 head",
    "unit": "hogs slaughtered Wednesday",
    "context": "USDA estimates packers killed 492,000 hogs Wednesday, against 484,335 a year ago. Cattle slaughter was 111,000 head."
  },
